   "definition_quote": "An adversarial bandit problem is specified by the number K of possible actions ... and by an assignment of rewards, i.e., an infinite sequence x(1), x(2), ... of vectors x(t) = (x_1(t),...,x_K(t)), where x_i(t) ∈ [0, 1] denotes the reward obtained if action i is chosen at time step t. ... We assume that the player knows the number K of actions."
